## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses incident leadership skills—specifically the ability to make quick, data-driven decisions under pressure while balancing product velocity with system reliability. It tests understanding of rollback versus patch tradeoffs and stakeholder management during high-stress situations.

## Key Concepts

- Ownership and accountability in incident response
- Data-driven decision making under pressure
- Stakeholder alignment and clear communication
- Risk assessment: rollback vs. patch tradeoffs

## Code Example

```javascript
function triage(telemetry) {
  const scope = assessScope(telemetry);
  const rootCause = identifyRootCause(scope);

  if (isLowRiskRollback()) {
    executeRollback();
  } else {
    deployKillSwitch();
  }

  communicateStakeholders(resolution);
  return monitorRecovery();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Interview context explanation focusing on ownership, bias-for-action, and customer obsession in high-stakes incidents across large platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Ownership: owning the outage end-to-end, not waiting for others
- Bias for Action: fast triage, interim fixes, clear cadences
- Customer Obsession: quantify impact, transparent communications, durable value

## Code Example

```javascript
function shouldTriage(metrics){
  const {latencyMs, errorRate, affectedRegions} = metrics;
  if(latencyMs > 2000 || errorRate > 0.02) return 'triage';
  if(affectedRegions.length > 0) return 'stakeholder-brief';
  return 'monitor';
}
```

